\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Thou didst leave Thy throne
\par And Thy kingly crown,
\par When Thou camest to earth for me;
\par But in Bethlehem's home
\par Was there found no room
\par For Thy holy nativity:
\par O come to my heart, Lord Jesus;
\par There is room in my heart for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Heaven's arches rang
\par When the angels sang,
\par Proclaiming Thy royal degree;
\par But of lowly birth
\par Cam'st  Thou Lord, on earth,
\par And in great humility;
\par O come to my heart, Lord Jesus;
\par There is room in my heart for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The foxes found rest,
\par And the birds their nest,
\par In the shade of the cedar-tree;
\par But Thy couch was the sod,
\par O Thou son of God,
\par In the deserts of Galilee,
\par O come to my heart, Lord Jesus
\par There is room in my heart for Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thou camest, O Lord,
\par With the living word
\par That should set Thy people free;
\par But, with mocking scorn
\par And with crown of thorn,
\par They bore Thee to Calvary;
\par O come to my heart, Lord Jesus;
\par Thy Cross is my only plea.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. When heaven's arches ring,
\par And her choirs shall sing,
\par At Thy coming to victory
\par Let Thy voice call me home,
\par Saying; Yet there is room,
\par There is room at My side for thee
\par And my heart shall rejoice, Lord Jesus,
\par When Thou comest and callest for me.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

